course: dictionary
lesson: 3080
title: Editor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An editor is a person whose job is to check, correct and improve writing before other people read it. When you check your own spelling and punctuation, you are doing a little editor's work.
explain: The word can also mean the person in charge of a newspaper or magazine. «An editor decides which stories are used, which go first and how long they are.» Those choices shape what people think is important.
explain: Editors work with films and videos too. Films are often shot out of order, so «the editor puts the shots in order afterwards». In computing, an editor is a program for changing text or code, which is why coders write in a code editor.
fact: An editor is a person who checks, corrects and improves writing before it is published.
fact: An editor can also be the person in charge of a newspaper, magazine or part of one.
fact: In films and videos, an editor cuts and joins the shots together.
fact: In computing, an editor is a program for changing text, pictures or code.
fact: «Editors» is the plural: one editor, two or more editors.
exercise: What is the main job of an editor? | Drawing pictures for the front cover | Selling copies in the shop | *Checking, correcting and improving writing before it is published | Hearing children read aloud
exercise: «Films are usually shot out of order, and the editor puts the shots in order afterwards.» When does the editor do this job? | On the set, while the camera is rolling | In the cinema, during the show | *Afterwards, when the shots are joined together | Before the film is written
exercise: «Coders write in a code editor.» What is a code editor? | A type of camera | A teacher who marks code | *A program for changing text or code | A printed book of rules
test: In your own writing, what would you do as an editor? | Make it longer, no matter what | Only write the title | Give it away without reading it | *Check spelling and punctuation, and improve the sentences
test: «An editor decides which stories are used, which go first and how long they are.» Which decision is this? | Choosing the colour of the paper | Choosing the font on a computer | *Choosing which stories go in and in what order | Choosing which camera to use
exam: What does the plural «editors» mean in «The school has two pupil editors»? | *Two or more people who check, correct and improve writing | Editor's | Editing | Edited
